   "text": {
    "L1": "Positive and negative tokens help us see integer operations.",
    "L2": "Here is a myth: two negatives always make a positive. That is not true for addition.",
    "L3": "A positive token and a negative token make a zero pair, so they cancel.",
    "L4": "For 5 plus negative 3, remove three zero pairs and two positive tokens remain.",
    "L5": "For subtraction, take tokens away. If there are not enough, add zero pairs first.",
    "L6": "Start with negative 2 and subtract 3. Add three zero pairs, then remove the three positives.",
    "L7": "Five negative tokens remain, so the answer is negative 5.",
    "L8": "On a number line, adding a positive moves right and adding a negative moves left. Now check the worked example."
   },
